matrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162017 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0d7f5df-a1f9-5242-9386-446313ec0178" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Columns of the First Matrix Given Part of a Singular Value Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1445126a-2e39-5f06-b93c-d37d24ee2f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418094} {:answer/id #uuid "53b67272-97c4-5cf9-9f1e-56b3cc74ec71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418102} {:answer/id #uuid "7c9664d0-c906-570b-a107-ae60f617c808" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418115} {:answer/id #uuid "c07ea98f-59b9-5163-8105-bf3d9c93e969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418128} {:answer/id #uuid "d1789205-39ba-5bd8-8e0e-afa42372c59c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53b67272-97c4-5cf9-9f1e-56b3cc74ec71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418102} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cefc262-fc57-5df7-b114-66f69510f234" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9020d5f8-c5f3-54dc-9474-2d2b14ec7c2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-96305" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A,$ $Σ,$ and $V$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ what is the first column of $U?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ and ${\\sigma }_{i}\\ne 0,$ then the $i$th column of $U$ can be found as\n\n$$\n{u}_{i}=\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{i}}A{v}_{i},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${v}_{i}$ is the $i$th column of the matrix $V.$\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that the singular values are ${\\sigma }_{1}=9$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=1.$ Therefore, the first column of $U$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{27}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371381 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162019 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9466d5b-d361-5504-8e16-99f87210e808" :knowledge-point/title "The Singular Value Decomposition of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c6eff25-c0fc-5cff-b89a-ea3df60bc57a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371383} {:answer/id #uuid "e891c291-46bc-51cc-90f8-4be4297699d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371384} {:answer/id #uuid "34122363-16d9-56df-9b3f-b02634a9a8a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371385} {:answer/id #uuid "f39d2e74-50cb-5515-aa8a-3fb01d053a03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371386} {:answer/id #uuid "0a333ced-2bf0-5916-b1d2-6bcfa569537f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c6eff25-c0fc-5cff-b89a-ea3df60bc57a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371383} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9c6dbf7-365b-568c-b7a1-8cd4a51005ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f93258a8-eb4b-5688-9b20-35af35814e98" :question/math-academy-id "q-96354" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}17 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 17\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=5$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=3.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=25,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-25I & =\\begin{bmatrix}17 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 17\\end{bmatrix}-25\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-25I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-9I & =\\begin{bmatrix}17 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 17\\end{bmatrix}-9\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-9I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404891 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162019 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9466d5b-d361-5504-8e16-99f87210e808" :knowledge-point/title "The Singular Value Decomposition of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4eaa68b-520c-58b4-a17b-57dd48766c58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404893} {:answer/id #uuid "dad029c8-f1bd-5774-bd9b-6cc44666c74f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404894} {:answer/id #uuid "b1179464-c161-5f17-9d1b-ec79fe124e14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} & \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} & -\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404895} {:answer/id #uuid "13acfcf7-36f6-5edb-88df-5d728cfbb0ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} & -\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} & -\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404896} {:answer/id #uuid "717ea9f0-7aa4-55d1-823a-4458379130c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13acfcf7-36f6-5edb-88df-5d728cfbb0ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} & -\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} & -\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404896} :answer-field/id #uuid "e29ceeea-5603-57fa-99fc-57e0cab72178" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5095a12c-e6f9-56a4-8ce5-1c1e4698b3dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-96360" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}65 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 80\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=9$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=8.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=81,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-81I & =\\begin{bmatrix}65 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 80\\end{bmatrix}-81\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-16 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-81I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=64,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-64I & =\\begin{bmatrix}65 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 80\\end{bmatrix}-64\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-64I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{36}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{32}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ -\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} & -\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} & -\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}]}
